  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "Variant_decodeJsonUnwrapExtensionObject",
    "file": "open62541/src/ua_types_encoding_json.c",
    "description": "On failure after allocating and decoding an unwrapped ExtensionObject body, the function calls `UA_free(dst->data)` but leaves `dst->data` pointing to the freed allocation (around lines 2977-2980). The error propagates to `UA_decodeJson`, whose generic cleanup calls `UA_deleteMembers`/`Variant_clear`; because the Variant still has a non-NULL `type` and dangling `data`, `Variant_clear` passes that pointer to `UA_Array_delete`, freeing it a second time. The vulnerable function must clear ownership state after freeing (and should perform type-aware cleanup for partially decoded data).",
    "conditions": "Decode attacker-controlled JSON as a `UA_Variant` whose `Type` is ExtensionObject (22), with a `Body` containing a resolvable `TypeId` and structure encoding (encoding absent/zero), so the helper changes the Variant type and allocates `dst->data`. The nested body must then be malformed or type-incompatible so `decodeFields` returns an error after allocation. In this PoV, `TypeId` numeric Id 5 resolves to a known built-in type, while the malformed/object body and trailing tokens cause decoding failure. The helper frees the allocation without nulling the pointer, and the propagated failure makes `UA_decodeJson` clean the Variant and double-free it."
  },
